\section{Derived Efficiency Metrics}
\label{sec:results_derived}

To capture the joint effect of throughput improvement and congestion reduction, we define composite metrics that better reflect overall network efficiency:

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Throughput efficiency}: $\text{TE} = \text{Throughput}_{/h} \;/\; \text{Congestion Index}$, measuring vehicles processed per unit of congestion.
    \item \textbf{Normalized waiting burden}: $\text{WA} = \text{Total Waiting Time} \;/\; N_{\text{arrived}}$, a normalized network-level waiting burden.
    \item \textbf{CO$_2$ per arrived vehicle}: $\text{CA} = \text{Total CO}_2 \;/\; N_{\text{arrived}}$, a normalized emissions burden per arrived vehicle.
\end{itemize}

Table~\ref{tab:derived_results} reports these derived metrics across controllers.

